public class CartState
{
    public List<string> Items { get; } = [];
    public event Action? OnChange;

    public void Add(string item)
    {
        Items.Add(item);
        OnChange?.Invoke();
    }
}
```

CartCount.razor, in the layout's header:

```razor
@inject CartState Cart

<span>Cart: @Cart.Items.Count</span>
```

ProductCard.razor, on the page:

```razor
@inject CartState Cart

<button @onclick="() => Cart.Add(Name)">Add</button>
```

Everything is interactive and `CartState` is scoped. The header shows **Cart: 0**. You click **Add** once.

**What does the header show right after the click?**

